\begin{align*}29 &\leq \lfloor x \lfloor x \rfloor \rfloor < \lfloor x \lfloor x \rfloor + x \rfloor < \lfloor x (\lfloor x \rfloor + 1) \rfloor = \lfloor x \lfloor x \rfloor \rfloor + \lfloor x \rfloor = 29 + \lfloor x \rfloor\end{align*}
Thus, $\lfloor x \rfloor = 28.$ Then, we want $29 \leq 28 x < 28 x + 28 < 29 + 28 = 57.$ We solve those inequalities to find $1.035714 \ldots < x \leq 1.035714 \ldots$. The answer is $28 < x \leq 28 + \frac{1}{28}.$ </think> <answer> $\boxed{28+\frac{1}{28}}$ </answer>

